            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="LES01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Charles Robert</forename>
                        <surname>Leslie</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1794-10-19">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1859-05-05"/>
                    <occupation>literary genre painter</occupation>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The <title>DNB</title> identifies his particular friends as including <persName key="IRV01">Washington Irving</persName>.  The meetings prior to 1820 
    are not coded on the grounds that the first set are before Leslie's arrival in England, and the 1816 group of entries are 
    associated very strongly with Godwin's trip to Edinburgh and to his relationship with the publisher Constable. Both sets seem likely to refer to <persName key="LES02">John Leslie</persName>. However, 
    the 1820 meetings begin by calling on Leslie with Irving, and the next dines with Irving and Leslie. The death of Leslie in 1832 refers to Sir John Leslie.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
